WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.819
Bajie waved his rake at the demon Golden Horn.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.203
"You'll never harm the Tang Monk!" shouted the pig.

3
00:00:08.204 --> 00:00:11.950
"My rake is very powerful!"

4
00:00:11.951 --> 00:00:16.579
[g@Bajie rushed toward Golden Horn.

5
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.562
But the demon was strong.@g]

6
00:00:20.563 --> 00:00:24.097
[g@Bajie was knocked out.

7
00:00:24.098 --> 00:00:33.928
When he woke up, he was tied up in a dark cave.@g]

8
00:00:33.929 --> 00:00:38.475
"Bajie is taking a long time to search the mountain," said the Tang Monk.

9
00:00:38.476 --> 00:00:45.845
"I hope he's okay."

10
00:00:45.846 --> 00:00:49.568
Wukong frowned. "He probably went back to sleep.

11
00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:52.321
I should have followed him again."

12
00:00:52.322 --> 00:00:55.057
[g@"Let's keep walking," said Wujing.

13
00:00:55.058 --> 00:00:57.906
"We'll find Bajie along the way."@g]

14
00:00:57.907 --> 00:01:01.129
"We must stay alert though," said Wukong.

15
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.896
"We still don't know if there are any demons on this mountain."

16
00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:07.702
[g@The group headed up the mountain.

17
00:01:07.703 --> 00:01:10.378
Soon they heard a voice.@g]

18
00:01:10.379 --> 00:01:12.758
"Help me!" cried a man.

19
00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:15.815
"Someone is in trouble," said the Tang Monk.

20
00:01:15.816 --> 00:01:22.825
He and his companions hurried ahead and found an old monk lying near the road.

21
00:01:22.826 --> 00:01:25.688
[g@"Thank goodness!" cried the old monk.

22
00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:28.030
"You must help me."@g]

23
00:01:28.031 --> 00:01:31.564
The Tang Monk got down from his horse.

24
00:01:31.565 --> 00:01:36.830
[g@"Of course we will help you," he said.

25
00:01:36.831 --> 00:01:38.618
"Please stand up."@g]

26
00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:41.320
[g@"I can't," said the old man.

27
00:01:41.321 --> 00:01:42.671
"My leg is injured.

28
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:44.353
It hurts terribly."@g]

29
00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:47.347
[g@He started to cry.

30
00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:51.501
"How will I ever get back home?"@g]

31
00:01:51.502 --> 00:01:54.197
"Please don't cry," said the Tang Monk.

32
00:01:54.198 --> 00:01:55.645
[g@"We will help you.

33
00:01:55.646 --> 00:01:57.664
How did your leg get hurt?"@g]

34
00:01:57.665 --> 00:02:01.451
"A tiger attacked me," said the old monk.

35
00:02:01.452 --> 00:02:05.162
Wukong looked suspiciously at the man.

36
00:02:05.163 --> 00:02:08.235
[g@"He isn't really a monk," he thought.

37
00:02:08.236 --> 00:02:10.804
"I'm sure he wants to harm Master.@g]

38
00:02:10.805 --> 00:02:14.271
But I can't tell Master that—he won't believe me."

39
00:02:14.272 --> 00:02:16.646
"Wukong," said the Tang Monk.

40
00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:22.211
"Please carry this poor monk down the mountain."

41
00:02:22.212 --> 00:02:25.914
Wukong walked over and picked up the old monk.

42
00:02:25.915 --> 00:02:28.510
"Ouch!" cried the monk.

43
00:02:28.511 --> 00:02:31.739
[g@"Be careful, Wukong," said the Tang Monk.

44
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.482
"His leg is hurt badly."@g]

45
00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:38.265
[g@The group continued along the road.

46
00:02:38.266 --> 00:02:41.136
Wukong carried the injured monk.@g]

47
00:02:41.137 --> 00:02:47.346
He walked slowly, letting the Tang Monk and Wujing go ahead.

48
00:02:47.347 --> 00:02:51.116
"I know you're really a demon," the monkey whispered.

49
00:02:51.117 --> 00:02:54.791
"And I know you want to eat the Tang Monk."

50
00:02:54.792 --> 00:02:58.365
"I don't know what you're talking about," said the monk.

51
00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:02.468
"I'm just a simple monk who was attacked by a tiger."

52
00:03:02.469 --> 00:03:06.616
Wukong laughed. "Do you know who I am?

53
00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:09.051
[g@I am Sun Wukong.

54
00:03:09.052 --> 00:03:12.307
Heaven's entire army couldn't defeat me.@g]

55
00:03:12.308 --> 00:03:15.872
You're going to wish you'd never tried to harm the Tang Monk."

56
00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:21.061
As Wukong talked, he felt a heavy weight pressing down on him.

57
00:03:21.062 --> 00:03:26.557
He glanced up and realized an entire mountain was balanced on top of his head.

58
00:03:26.558 --> 00:03:29.071
The monkey laughed again.

59
00:03:29.072 --> 00:03:32.998
"So you're going to use magic tricks to trap me under a mountain?

60
00:03:32.999 --> 00:03:38.400
Well, let me tell you—Buddha himself once trapped me under a mountain.

61
00:03:38.401 --> 00:03:41.171
And I was able to lift it."

62
00:03:41.172 --> 00:03:44.020
Wukong felt more weight.

63
00:03:44.021 --> 00:03:47.559
[g@Now he had two mountains on top of him.

64
00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.161
He walked more slowly.@g]

65
00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:54.304
"This still isn't enough weight to stop me," he said.

66
00:03:54.305 --> 00:03:59.445
"Now that the Tang Monk isn't around, I should clobber you with my iron bar."

67
00:03:59.446 --> 00:04:02.809
Suddenly the old monk vanished.

68
00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.786
A third mountain appeared on top of the first two.

69
00:04:06.787 --> 00:04:12.921
Wukong's knees buckled, and all three mountains crashed down on top of him.

70
00:04:12.922 --> 00:04:15.319
The monkey was trapped.

71
00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.938
The old monk appeared again.

72
00:04:17.939 --> 00:04:24.712
There was a flash of light as he changed back into his demon form.

73
00:04:24.713 --> 00:04:27.753
Golden Horn laughed with delight.

74
00:04:27.754 --> 00:04:31.955
"Wukong was the most powerful of these travelers.

75
00:04:31.956 --> 00:04:35.545
[g@It will be easy to defeat Wujing.

76
00:04:35.546 --> 00:04:43.997
Tonight I will dine on the Tang Monk!"@g]

